**Most of the distance between Table 3 and the current results is the scoring and the configuration choice, not the models. The rest is split between real model differences and a harder task set.**

- **Scoring and selection (5.1).** Removing the differences one at a time takes Claude Sonnet 4.5 from 0.80 to 0.22, Gemini 2.5 Pro from 0.66 to 0.33 and GPT-5 from 0.67 to 0.43, on the same answers:
  - picking the best of 18 configurations adds 0.05–0.13 (0.13 for Sonnet, whose best configuration rests on 3 answers);
  - answers to properties that were not asked (the airport's `name`, `city`, `country`, mostly right once the airport is recognised) add up to 0.13 (Sonnet, Gemini Flash, Haiku; nothing for GPT-5, which answers only what is asked);
  - values copied from the input add 0.13 for Qwen and almost nothing for the proprietary models;
  - the stricter tolerance changes little and mostly *raises* the score (lone coordinates are compared instead of skipped);
  - **counting abstentions is the largest single step**: −0.19 to −0.36. Sonnet abstains on 63% of the asked properties, which the DOLAP F1 ignores.
- **Precision is 1 by construction (5.2).** The DOLAP notebook calls sklearn with `y_true` all ones, so a wrong answer can never be a false positive. It is the same mechanism as our F1 ign: F1 ign = 2P/(1+P) is the DOLAP F1 restricted to the asked properties. With wrong answers counted, the precision of the proprietary models is 0.25–0.54.
- **Models (5.3).** On the same 36 tasks with our scoring, the proprietary models span F1 0.17–0.43: GPT-5 (0.43) and GPT-5 Mini (0.38) are clearly ahead, Gemini 0.28–0.33, and the two Claude models 0.17–0.22. gemma4:31b (1-run test) reaches 0.19, the level of the Claude models; Qwen3 4B 0.10. Being proprietary is not enough to score high; the GPT-5 models are the ones that stand out.
- **Task set (5.4).** The v5 task set is harder than the DOLAP one:
  - `commercial_flights` is about a third of the scored v5 properties (2% in DOLAP) and almost never found (recall 0.03–0.08); without it the lineup's F1 on v5 rises by 0.05–0.08;
  - with context, G names the airport in 30% of v5 tasks against 58% in DOLAP. When G names it, the lineup's F1 is 0.20–0.34 (context on) and 0.22–0.41 (context off), within the range of the proprietary models on the DOLAP tasks;
  - v5 also includes airports without routes (rank 3,227 of 7,698), but in v5 F1 is the same across centrality strata (0.17–0.19), so this does not explain the gap.
- **What can be said now:** the paper's numbers are not comparable with ours. Scored the same way, the proprietary models are 0.17–0.43 on the DOLAP tasks and the lineup 0.14–0.34 on v5. The direct comparison on the same tasks needs the lineup's runs (section 2), which are waiting for Ollama credits.
